{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:21:49.280Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"81d0d6155c8486cbca12e0e326a8fedbc543a4804df43a71f1fdbe1198799d57","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's four Coastal digests. Only a few items are on these two accounts, and one ticket number is ambiguous.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast)**\n- **#4419:** The `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It is still open, per Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. See the caveat below.\n- **PD-8841:** Chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B. It comes from your own 2025-12-08 cutover recap, not from Moss's notes or the channels.\n- **No ticket number:**\n  - Chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change is the main friction point (cheat sheet).\n  - The Berth 2 yard map CSV import bug is in your recap.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882:** Warehouse managers asked for a bulk-clear button for departed barges (cheat sheet).\n- **#4419:** Moss's 11/2/2025 digest also lists this number, for a barge slip 7 schedule sync on Kwame's port account. Driftmoor asked for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift.\n- **No ticket number:** The tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch (cheat sheet).\n\n**Caveat on #4419:** The cheat sheet ties it to PHL's report timeout. The 11/2 digest ties it to Driftmoor's slip 7 sync. Moss's notes don't say which is right, so Kwame should confirm before the review. I've listed it under both accounts rather than pick one.\n\n**Left out as Pellow Home Living (or other accounts):**\n- #8812, the Door 4B scanner at Hagerstown, and PD-4821, the door 6 maintenance block.\n- PD-4827 and PD-4824, which are Saltmarsh tickets.\n\nI found nothing on PHL or Driftmoor in #coastal-random, and the #coastal-team posts from Oct 2025 to Feb 2026 are about Saltmarsh and the PHL naming mix-up. I can only see what's in those channels and the shared notes. If a ticket was logged in a tool I can't see, it won't be on this list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
